### Keep snapshot disposal off the finalizer thread (1/2)

**Severity:** `medium`

When this safety-net finalizer releases the wrapper's last snapshot lease, the callback can synchronously reach the extension-backed snapshot's `Dispose()`. If that call blocks, it stalls CLR finalizer processing. Add a lazy, bounded `DedicatedThreadPool` so blocking extension cleanup does not consume a shared ThreadPool worker.

```suggestion
    private static readonly Lazy<DedicatedThreadPool> _finalizerDisposalPool = new(
        () => new DedicatedThreadPool(minThreads: 1, maxThreads: 8, name: "FallbackFinalizer"));

    private readonly IDictionary<string, object> _extendedProperties;
```

### Keep snapshot disposal off the finalizer thread (2/2)

**Severity:** `medium`

After adding the dedicated pool, enqueue the exchanged lease's `Dispose` method on it instead of invoking it inline. This keeps the finalizer from waiting for extension disposal while keeping the blocking call off the shared ThreadPool; please apply both grouped suggestions together.

```suggestion
        var materializationLease = Interlocked.Exchange(ref _materializationLease, null);
        if (materializationLease is not null)
        {
            _ = _finalizerDisposalPool.Value.QueueAsync(materializationLease.Dispose);
        }
```
